<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burma, now Myanmar, is a country in mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> fought a series of costly and unsuccessful wars against Burma in the 1760s. Burma was annexed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> in the nineteenth century, conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 1942, and became independent in 1948 during British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decolonisation">decolonisation</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burma.jpg" alt="Burma" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Myanmar.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
